From d3bd3d63c270670da7ffbcff4afa1b814d31f7b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Aleksandr.Khlebnikov" <aleksandr.khlebnikov@wirenboard.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:37:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Repost the original message after an admin unbans its author

--message.restore / MESSAGE_RESTORE: when an admin presses unban on a ban report,
the bot posts the text of the deleted message back to the primary chat, addressed
to its author with a text_mention and prefixed with this message. Empty disables
it. Training and dry modes never delete the message, so nothing is reposted there.

Without it a wrongly banned author is unrestricted, but the question is gone and
nothing tells them to ask again: with NO_SPAM_REPLY the chat never saw a word
about the ban.

The logic lives in its own file and sends with an entity rather than a parse
mode, so the rest of the change is a few one-line hooks.
